{"kind": "report", "step": 17, "ts": "2026-11-19T02:20:53.076567+00:00", "data": {"category": "wan", "host": "gw.lan", "component": "wan_link", "cause": "The internet link died when the cable modem lost upstream sync with the provider plant at 02:01:44 (\"No Ranging Response received - T3 time-out\", then a TFTP config-file failure before it finally re-registered at 02:28:21); the modem is now back to OPERATIONAL but the firewall's WAN side was never reconfigured during the outage \u2014 the watchdog runs in observe mode and only logged \"would_reload\" \u2014 so vtnet0 still cannot carry traffic to the ISP gateway.", "evidence": ["ping -c 3 -n -q 198.51.100.1 on gw.lan: 3 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss \u2014 no reachability to the ISP gateway even though ARP shows it (arp -a -n: 198.51.100.1 at 00:17:10:9a:a3:96 on vtnet0).", "ifconfig vtnet0: UP,RUNNING,LOWER_UP, inet 198.51.100.27 \u2014 physical/WAN interface itself is up, so this is not a dead NIC or cable on the firewall.", "netstat -rn: default route present via 198.51.100.1 on vtnet0; /var/db/dhclient.leases.vtnet0 holds lease 198.51.100.27 with server-identifier 203.0.113.67 and renew time 2026/3/5 \u2014 i.e. the WAN config was never refreshed during this outage.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-events.jsonl: 02:01:44 id 82000200 'No Ranging Response received - T3 time-out'; 02:14:10 id 68000407 'TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND'; 02:28:21 id 90000000 'Cable Modem Reboot because of - unknown; registration complete' \u2014 outage began with loss of provider-side sync and only completed re-registration at 02:28.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/events.jsonl: outage_start 02:06 (mode observe); decision action=none reason=modem_not_operational (cm_status NOT_SYNCHRONIZED) at 02:06; then modem_settling at 02:29, and reload decisions at 02:30 and 02:40 recorded only as 'would_reload' \u2014 no actual reload happened.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/state.json: outage_start 1772521560, reloads_in_outage 2, last_reload 1772523600, modem_op_since 1772522940 \u2014 the modem has been operational for ~12 minutes while the WAN is still down.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-metrics.jsonl: uncorrected codewords climbing 0 -> 112 -> 131 and corrected 40211 -> 52070 during the event, worst_uncorrected 615 \u2014 degraded provider plant behind the de-sync."], "action": "change_config", "recommendation": "Reload/renew the firewall's WAN interface (vtnet0) now that the modem reports OPERATIONAL and has re-registered, so it picks up a fresh lease and re-establishes the path to 198.51.100.1; there is no need to reboot the modem again since it already completed registration. Afterwards, have the watchdog act on its own reload decision instead of only observing, and ask the ISP about the upstream T3/ranging loss and rising uncorrected codewords on the plant.", "detail": "WAN stalled after ISP-side modem de-sync and re-registration", "fix": "wan_reload", "contributing": {"host": "gw.lan", "component": "monitoring_config"}}}
